IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc19-s492-25`

-- ccc19-tests-s492-25.l4 -- tests for ccc19-s492-25.l4 (Criminal Code (Canada) s 492.25, Notice to Victims).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the subsection named beside it, before the run. A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `s 492.25(1) -- If an application for a finding of unreasonable delay is filed with the court, the prosecutor shall ... take reasonable steps to inform any victim`

-- filed, a victim exists: the duty
#ASSERT `s 492.25(1) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the filing` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not filed: the "If" is not met
#ASSERT `s 492.25(1) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the filing` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.25(1) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the filing` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- filed, no victim: "any victim" is a scope and the text does not say what follows: not covered
#ASSERT `s 492.25(1) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the filing` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- filed, and the section 2 definition of victim does not settle the case (the seam answers NOTHING): not covered, carried through
#ASSERT `s 492.25(1) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the filing` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative rule. Expected, from the text: a duty on the prosecutor that stands until performed (no period is stated); performed, FULFILLED; no filing or no victim, nothing owed.
-- Duty arises, nothing done yet: the standing obligation (no WITHIN, so no breach however long the clock runs).
#TRACE `s 492.25(1) the duty of the prosecutor to inform the victims of the filing` TRUE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- Duty arises, the prosecutor takes the steps: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 492.25(1) the duty of the prosecutor to inform the victims of the filing` TRUE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 492.25(1) take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the filing of the application` AT 3

-- No filing: nothing owed.
#TRACE `s 492.25(1) the duty of the prosecutor to inform the victims of the filing` FALSE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- Filed but no victim: not covered, so the rule states no duty.
#TRACE `s 492.25(1) the duty of the prosecutor to inform the victims of the filing` TRUE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

§ `s 492.25(2) -- The court shall, at the time the application is heard, inquire of the prosecutor`

#ASSERT `s 492.25(2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not at the time the application is heard
#ASSERT `s 492.25(2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- At the hearing, nothing done yet: the standing obligation on the court.
#TRACE `s 492.25(2) the duty of the court to inquire of the prosecutor` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

-- At the hearing, the court inquires: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 492.25(2) the duty of the court to inquire of the prosecutor` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 492.25(2) inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the filing of the application` AT 1

-- Not at the hearing: nothing owed.
#TRACE `s 492.25(2) the duty of the court to inquire of the prosecutor` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

§ `s 492.25(3) -- The prosecutor shall, as soon as feasible after a decision has been made on the application, take reasonable steps to inform the victims, if any, of the decision`

#ASSERT `s 492.25(3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the decision` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no decision yet: "after a decision has been made"
#ASSERT `s 492.25(3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the decision` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- decided, no victims: "the victims, if any"
#ASSERT `s 492.25(3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the decision` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.25(3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the decision` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- decided, and the section 2 definition of victim does not settle the case: not covered
#ASSERT `s 492.25(3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the decision` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- Decided, victims exist, nothing done: the standing obligation.
#TRACE `s 492.25(3) the duty of the prosecutor to inform the victims of the decision` TRUE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 90)

-- Decided, victims exist, the prosecutor informs them: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 492.25(3) the duty of the prosecutor to inform the victims of the decision` TRUE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 492.25(3) take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the decision on the application` AT 2

-- No decision yet: nothing owed.
#TRACE `s 492.25(3) the duty of the prosecutor to inform the victims of the decision` FALSE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 90)

§ `s 492.25(4) -- the prosecutor's failure to inform the victims of the application does not preclude the court from making a decision`

-- a failure to take reasonable steps: the text says it does not preclude the court
#ASSERT `s 492.25(4) the failure of the prosecutor precludes the court from making a decision on the application` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no such failure: the subsection does not speak
#ASSERT `s 492.25(4) the failure of the prosecutor precludes the court from making a decision on the application` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
